# Lint + formal sequential equivalence of mac_baseline and mac_opiso (Yosys).
# The miter compares all outputs every cycle. sat -seq 10 proves (bounded model
# check) that they match in every cycle of every input sequence of 10 cycles
# starting from the all-zero state (= the reset state of both designs).
# An unbounded proof (sat -tempinduct) did not converge in 15+ minutes: the
# induction step reduces to SAT equivalence of two multiplier copies.
# Run from the repository root:  yosys -s scripts/equiv.ys
read_verilog -sv rtl/mac_baseline.sv rtl/mac_opiso.sv
hierarchy -check
proc
check -assert
miter -equiv -flatten -make_outputs mac_baseline mac_opiso miter
hierarchy -top miter
opt_clean
dffunmap
sat -verify -seq 10 -prove trigger 0 -set-init-zero miter
